{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird","id":1518277,"title":"The hatred the other splats have for Vampires is weird","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-18T17:19:09-07:00","id":1518277,"title":"The hatred the other splats have for Vampires is weird","content":"Vampires are pretty hated by everything and everyone. Mages, Fera, Demons, Changelings, Spirits, etc.<br /> <br /> Other than the fact that any criticism thrown at vampires can easily be reflected back to the other splats, who at times have done way worse. It's just kind of weird. Why have VTM a part of the same universe? Especially when it's quite clear that every other splat seems to just want to exterminate them, and could easily do so if they set aside their differences, which doesn't seem that unlikely to happen due to their immense loathing for them. Also, why allow any access to the middle umbra when its denizens for some incoherent reason also hate vampires?<br /> <br /> IDK, feels kind of weird.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T17:31:49-07:00","id":1518278,"title":"","content":"It's not really the doing of the other games. V:tM set down the setting element of &quot;lupines kill vampires who try to go out into the wilderness&quot; back in the first green marble book, and everything just followed from there. The setting details of, say, W:tA only flesh out the Vampire-specified setting element (that being that Kindred act like BSDs, which no one wants to be around due with ill spiritual shit that follows them around a compounded issue, so Garou and Fera avoid them most times and end them when possible).<br /> <br /> As to why have them be in the same setting? I ask that a lot myself, but for different reasons. Mostly, I think that the foundational work just wanted vampires to be full of angst all the time and this was just another way to do it. Also, later W:tA specifies that vampires <i>cannot</i> enter the Middle Umbra; if a power from V:tM says that it allows a trip to the Umbra, the Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook reroutes them to the Dark Umbra, maybe the Astral, never the Penumbra familiar to W:tA. Even if you don't op[t for this, however, it's worth noting that crossover into W:tA is fucking around until you find out. Nothing is resilient enough to deal with the splatter horror setting of W:tA but characters from W:tA, where a form that can soak agg is standard and Rage or something like it usually is, as well. This is not a fault or W:tA, or something wrong with it, unlike what the development directives of W5 apparently thought; it's a fundamentally different game, and this setup can be taken as just another reason why Garou and Fera generally view vampires as lower priority targets than ferectoi and other fomori, BSDs, or banes and cults dedicated to banes, if you have to keep them in the same world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T18:03:24-07:00","id":1518279,"title":"","content":"Should other splats be <i>welcoming</i> of the ambulatory corpses that steal the blood of innocents just to survive? Whose powers seem custom built to predate upon, manipulate, and exploit normal humans (including the humans you like)? Who seem to only catch the attention of other supernaturals when they're doing decided monstrous things? (To the point an entire sect of them - the least caring of secrecy, mind - openly reject all matters of ethics or humanity, and choose to commit atrocities because they think it's fun).<br /> <br /> While less-evil vampires exist, from an outsider's perspective, it certainly <i>looks</i> like vampires are all diabolical parasites. Creatures whose very existence is a literal drain on the lives of normal people, and seem disinterested in seeking alternatives (if, indeed, any alternatives to that unlifestyle are even possible, for as far as outsiders know).<br /> <br /> All of this before you get into specifics. Like how vampires generally &quot;read&quot; as Wyrm-tainted to Garou (those who don't tend to be overlooked). Or how Mages tend to have very well developed and firmly held belief systems, and thus have very strong opinions about blood-drinking cadavers that spurn the light and corrupt Sleepers for their own myriad ends. Or how Wraiths might have a natural antipathy towards vampires, since the latter so often MAKE the former through murder (and also have just enough necromancers, that actively <i>enslave</i> Wraiths, to be a big red flag). Or how the entire point of monster hunters (capital-H and lowercase h) is to protect mortals from the supernatural predators stalking them, or to get revenge for loved ones lost thereof. Or how Mummies might see vampires as their only &quot;real&quot; competition in the game of eons.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, vampires engage in a lot of &quot;social engineering&quot; (read: conspiratorial manipulation/mind control), that ends up causing wide-spread negative effects. Not because they're fighting (or serving) the Wyrm, or because they seek to affect the Consensus in a way that makes their vision of Reality come to fruition. But seemingly for no other reason than personal power and gratification, and to spite a rival. A Syndicate member of the Technocracy will push policies that leave thousands homeless and municipal programs underfunded because he genuinely believes in Capitalism (the idiot). A vampire will do those same things because homeless people with no access to shelters or even functioning street lights <i>are easier to feed on</i>.<br /> <br /> In that light, it would be weird if everyone else <i>didn't </i>hate vampires. Splats dislike/distrust other splats (and rival factions within their splat) at the best of times. But vampires are arguably on a whole other level, just at their base layer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T18:34:18-07:00","id":1518281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518279#post1518279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should other splats be <i>welcoming</i> of the ambulatory corpses that steal the blood of innocents just to survive? Whose powers seem custom built to predate upon, manipulate, and exploit normal humans (including the humans you like)? Who seem to only catch the attention of other supernaturals when they're doing decided monstrous things? (To the point an entire sect of them - the least caring of secrecy, mind - openly reject all matters of ethics or humanity, and choose to commit atrocities because they think it's fun).<br /> <br /> While less-evil vampires exist, from an outsider's perspective, it certainly <i>looks</i> like vampires are all diabolical parasites. Creatures whose very existence is a literal drain on the lives of normal people, and seem disinterested in seeking alternatives (if, indeed, any alternatives to that unlifestyle are even possible, for as far as outsiders know).<br /> <br /> All of this before you get into specifics. Like how vampires generally &quot;read&quot; as Wyrm-tainted to Garou (those who don't tend to be overlooked). Or how Mages tend to have very well developed and firmly held belief systems, and thus have very strong opinions about blood-drinking cadavers that spurn the light and corrupt Sleepers for their own myriad ends. Or how Wraiths might have a natural antipathy towards vampires, since the latter so often MAKE the former through murder (and also have just enough necromancers, that actively <i>enslave</i> Wraiths, to be a big red flag). Or how the entire point of monster hunters (capital-H and lowercase h) is to protect mortals from the supernatural predators stalking them, or to get revenge for loved ones lost thereof. Or how Mummies might see vampires as their only &quot;real&quot; competition in the game of eons.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, vampires engage in a lot of &quot;social engineering&quot; (read: conspiratorial manipulation/mind control), that ends up causing wide-spread negative effects. Not because they're fighting (or serving) the Wyrm, or because they seek to affect the Consensus in a way that makes their vision of Reality come to fruition. But seemingly for no other reason than personal power and gratification, and to spite a rival. A Syndicate member of the Technocracy will push policies that leave thousands homeless and municipal programs underfunded because he genuinely believes in Capitalism (the idiot). A vampire will do those same things because homeless people with no access to shelters or even functioning street lights <i>are easier to feed on</i>.<br /> <br /> In that light, it would be weird if everyone else <i>didn't </i>hate vampires. Splats dislike/distrust other splats (and rival factions within their splat) at the best of times. But vampires are arguably on a whole other level, just at their base layer.</div> </div> </div> </div>These criticisms can easily be reflected back to the other splats. Specifically WTA, MTA, DTF, and WTO. Besides the Blood drinking, they all have a faction that manipulate, exploit humans, social engineer stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T18:47:39-07:00","id":1518284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518281#post1518281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These criticisms can easily be reflected back to the other splats. Specifically WTA, MTA, DTF, and WTO. Besides the Blood drinking, they all have a faction that manipulate, exploit humans, social engineer stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood drinking also automatically converts said blood to a drug that they can (and often do) use to addict, corrupt, and enslave anyone that they can get to drink it. That tends to make them nearly literal toxic waste people, and knowing anything about them would make anyone extremely hesitant to accept any kind of &quot;help&quot; from them, particularly if it's anywhere that the vampire can place their additives in food or drink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:53:21-07:00","id":1518290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518284#post1518284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood drinking also automatically converts said blood to a drug that they can (and often do) use to addict, corrupt, and enslave anyone that they can get to drink it. That tends to make them nearly literal toxic waste people, and knowing anything about them would make anyone extremely hesitant to accept any kind of &quot;help&quot; from them, particularly if it's anywhere that the vampire can place their additives in food or drink.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember, it's usually done for ghouling specific targets or blood bonding other vampires. No one is going around trying to make it a large scale practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T20:21:59-07:00","id":1518292,"title":"","content":"I mean the problem is Vampires hunt humans to feed off of, and sometimes killing their victims. It's not exactly a surprise that other beings, who are going to be preyed on vampires or see their family members, friends or other loved ones be preyed on by vampires, aren't huge fans of vampires. Other splats - werewolves, mages, changelings, etc, generally don't eat or hurt humans in the same way that vampires do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T20:40:22-07:00","id":1518293,"title":"","content":"Each has its reasons.<br /> <br /> Fera: Apparently they smell the Wyrm and because they are dead they that still &quot;alive&quot; apparently they have a connection with it, and we that know of the lore know this isn't true, but they don't and the fact that many of them interfere in the economy, policy and in some cases are associated with Pentex, doesn't help. Another point that is important to point out is that vampires can bind people in blood ties and addict them to their kisses, this by itself could be associated with the Wyrm that corrupts, but the problem really appears when they do this with one kinfolk or another. Fera, you probaly know why, in closing those who are related to Helios believe he cursed vampires and that's why they can't even touch sunlight, so they hate them.<br /> <br /> Mage: This one is more complicated because I imagine the two don't have a direct relationship, I believe that apart from the Tremere and maybe the Hecata, and of course the Celestial Core (And I think the Euthanatos too), one side has no interest or rivalry on the other, except when a vampire wants to bind a mage in a blood bond, or a mage wants to experiment on a vampire, but otherwise I think they see vampires as an anomaly and maybe a menace.<br /> <br /> Changeling: Changelings see vampires as another type of Changeling, a troublesome one, who absorbs glamor through blood or just feeds differently, in the same way that other changelings can be dangerous/problematic for their own species, especially Redcaps, vampires are also, apart from that there are vampires who hunt fairies. As a highlight, the fairies make mention of an enemy called the Formorian that reminds the Formori of the WTA so it is possible assumed that they may hate vampires by association.<br /> <br /> Demons: Those I don't think are really interested, but maybe they don't like Cainites by association with Cain? Or maybe it's because those who dislike humans see them as just another problem that humanity has caused to itself, whereas those who do see them as corruptors and one of the causes of humanity's downfall or one of it's consequences, is their fault and their need to end this or just ignores out for pity or shame.<br /> <br /> Wraith: I guess, because they're afraid because vampires can use necromancy and make their &quot;life&quot; hell, okay not all vampires do that, but the Wraith don't know that.<br /> <br /> Basically that's it I think, I'm sure I forgot something, but it should give you an idea. As for their uncooperative part, remember that many of them don't even know each other well, and people tend to fear what they don't know, they don't like vampires, but that doesn't mean they're good with others.\u200b Developing more than that would make this comment too long, but I can try if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T20:51:32-07:00","id":1518294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518281#post1518281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These criticisms can easily be reflected back to the other splats. Specifically WTA, MTA, DTF, and WTO. Besides the Blood drinking, they all have a faction that manipulate, exploit humans, social engineer stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are not equivalent, though. Neither in kind nor degree.<br /> <br /> By your admission, other splats have &quot;a faction&quot; that manipulates and exploits humans. Vampires <i>at large</i> do this as a rule. It's how their &quot;species&quot; operates, as far as most other splats are concerned. Even the relatively less evil vampire sects, like the Anarchs, still keep ghouls, gain influence over institutions, mind control, murder (or mind wipe) witnesses, and <i>hunt people for sustenance</i>. Vampires that feed exclusively on animals are a vanishingly tiny minority. Which means most vampires, sooner or later, kill innocent people via overfeeding, for malice, gluttony, apathy, or carelessness.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I need to reiterate the point I made in my earlier post: this is the behavior other splats are most likely to learn about. Vampires that maintain morally defensible unlives rarely pop up on anyone's radar. If a member of another splat has their attention on a vampire, it's usually because the vampire has caused problems as a direct result of the above. Most people in the other splats ONLY know of vampires as forces of corruption, predation, and violence.<br /> <br /> Why, then, would they think any different? Why give the benefit of the doubt to the <i>undead leeches</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> (One last point, RE: the other splats also being guilty of many sins of vampires. Okay, so? Yeah, other splats have hypocrites among them. <i>And?</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T23:09:35-07:00","id":1518296,"title":"","content":"If you have any concern for humanity then it's hard to approve of vampires. They're not only feeding on humanity but corrupting it. Even on a individual basis the damage being turned into a vampire does to a person is cataclysmic. <br /> you can usually argue you're own side has issues but outside of the vilest of the vile you can at least rationalise it. The union ultimately wish to uplift humanity, red talons want to save the planet etc. By contrast a vampires default is corruption, violation and murder and that's the nicer ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T23:28:13-07:00","id":1518298,"title":"","content":"Hate is a very strong word<br /> Let put aside Kindred of the East and Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom (and probably the Drowned Legacies), because those have a different relationship with the locals, so focus on our Cainite friends of Europe and most of the USA<br /> So the &quot;standard&quot; vampires/Cainites of WoD<br /> <br /> <b>The</b> <b>Werewolf </b>have their history with the Vampires<br /> If they are Lupin in the Game for that<br /> And if they are Garou... oh boy, for that.<br /> The Garou hate everything that is not a Garou, and even other Garou most of the time. They are full of prejudice and Rage and more often than not are the victim of a very strong conditioning, like in a cult. To the point different Spets consider each other idiots and it takes a little effort to a Tribe to exterminate another...<br /> Or whole species.<br /> From the Garou perspecitve, if they don't know better, the Leeches are a type of Fomori, or the descendants o the Bloody Man (who caused the whole problem with the Wyrm), but in essence represent everything tha is wrong with humanity. Not to mention they are more Weaver then Wyrm, the unliving proof, the problem is actually the Weaver and they spent their time fighting the &quot;wrong&quot; enemy<br /> I wouldn't say the Garou hate the vampires, not more than any other thing,- well some cases they do, like with the Followers of Set and the Silent Stirder or anyone who know what the hell the Tzimsice Koldun are capable of and they do better job cleaning out &quot;kupalas/Banes&quot; than they do - BUT if they are capable to see pass their conditioning? Cordial working relationship exist, like the Ventrue and the Glass Walkers and Siegfried of Vancouver who worked out the Covenant, a peace treaty between the local Kindred and the Lupines. In exchange for aiding in reforestation attempts and fighting against resource exploitation, the Lupines would guard his domain from any unwanted intruders and would refrain from unprovoked violence against vampires under Siegfried's protection -aruagbly the greaest achivement in history regarding of progress, the only time the Garou really achivemed anything in World of Drakness....<br /> The hate is there, sure, but is is a bit cultural misunderstanding based and the lack of ability to change from both part. But once they manage to move beyond that? The relationship could be frightingly effective and this fact scares the living/unliving shit out of both parites<br /> <br /> <b>The fae</b> tend to avoid the Kindred. Most vampires make Changelings uncomfortable, and most Changelings make vampires hungry. However, chance encounters do occur, and some Sluagh and Redcaps feel a certain kinship with the blood-drinking Prodigals.<br /> Not to mention the Kiasyd are a &quot;bridge&quot; between the two species, some even consider them as their own (and the Malkavians... depending of the edition or the Daugters of Cacophony, depending of their origin; in one have a strong ties to the Fae)<br /> And the Unseelie have a very open mind...<br /> The Elders are aware of them and respect the boundaries. For example the clan elders were displeased with the results of Marconius, but not <i>with </i>Marconius, who probably was tricked into drinking the tainted blood, and not with the other two Lasombra who worked with him, but because of the unauthorized blood experimentation, trafficking with a mage (and not even learning his name?!), and <i>possibly</i> angering the fae community. They left him alive and only banished him in the depths of an oubliette within Castel d'Ombro becasue no one wanted to possibly anger the Fae Lords who may or may not have ties with Marconius.<br /> It is not really hate from the Changeling part but more of a curious fear and uncomfortability. Or very deep fear when a changeling relise Chimerstry is a very lethal weapon and may inflict Chimercal Damage upon Changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b>s can kind of do anything they want so pretty much anything works here. A nephandus trying to recruit vampires for his infernal lord all the way up to a Celestial Chorus mage preaching to the ones Yaweh bas cursed. Certain Mages, notably Chakrivanti and some Verbena, will probably attack vampires on sight. The Order of Hermes has a long and complicated relationship with vampires (*cough* Tremere *cough* ). The Technocracy, who will capture, torture, interrogate, and repeatedly vivisect vampires for research, and then throw them in an incinerator once they've served their purpose. Or they might just purchase the local Camarilla and use it as a money laundering front, it really does depend.<br /> Still other magi simply don't care; I can't really see the consensus among Virtual Adepts or Hollow Ones being that vampires need to die on sight.<br /> Keep in mind, the upper eichelons of mages are essentially gods held back by their paradox leashes <i>however</i> they\u2019re also held back by hubris. Mages can also be omnipresent but not omniscient!<br /> Whenever there is supernatural activity eventually the mages will show up. They have an interest in monitoring all the magic and weird stuff around their territory. Vampires fear and distrust mages because mages are powerful and unpredictable, so I kind of becomes a cold war standoff.<br /> So in this case too, it wouldn't be hate per see, but fear, distrust and general curiosity between the two parties\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>The Fallen</b>... well... The War of Wrath changed the world in ways. Many blasphemous creatures were created, by accident or design, and in the depths of their anger and hatred, the rebels experimented on uncounted humans in the depths of their fortress, spawning abominations whose ultimate fate no one knows. Such could be the origin of the creatures haunting the earth in its present nights, feeding on the blood of mortals while spinning webs of influence and deceit across the entire globe. Some believe the vampires to be debased descendants of the nephilim, forced to sustain their superhuman powers through consumption of human blood. Others have learned of the vampires\u2019 own beliefs, that point to themselves as descendants of the First Murderer, none other than Caine himself. Those fallen who have heard the legend have no trouble believing such a thing is possible - they know all too well how cruel a vengeful Creator can be.<br /> Demons and the kindred are competitors for the same prize - mankind and all it has to offer. Both groups are highly territorial, prideful and more than willing to resort to violence if threatened. It\u2019s not surprising, then, that most demon-vampire relations tend to be highly confrontational. This is especially true when a fallen and one of the kindred find themselves vying for a hold over a particular mortal or mortal institution. Both sides will spare no effort to protect what they see as theirs. So far, any attempts at d\u00e9tente between a kindred court and an infernal court in a given town or city have broken down into outright conflict, continuing until one side or another is destroyed or leaves for safer climes.<br /> This is not to say that all demon-vampire relations are ultimately destructive. Some of the fallen, particularly of the Reconciler faction, have forged ties with individual vampires, hoping to use their lore to restore the kindred\u2019s humanity in exchange for knowledge and support as the demons try to further their agenda worldwide.<br /> It wouldn't be hate, and in a sense, pity and even kinship; after all the Fallen Elohim were cursed to become the Sebettu by Michael... and the Archangels (not God, mind you) cursed Caine who passed it own to his descendants.<br /> Strange kinship feeling and pity, paired with the history of Infernalism and their similar nature makes the contanct and mutual feeling is uneasy at best but not hate really, no.<br /> Well except when the Salubri warriors comes in to the picture who are the undead insturments of God and with the Blooding Cereminy takes up the Celestial Name of an Angel and call upon the Host's power. Around that time (and if the Lasombra Abyss is the same of the primodial one) the excrement hit the fanning plam leaf<br /> <br /> <b>The Wraith </b>are... they know. But hate? I wouldn't say that.<br /> Some of them are wraith because a feeding went wrong and/or a Vampire lost it and a killing spree<br /> Vampire have a bit more interaction with a Wraith.<br /> The Merit is &quot;Spirit Mentor&quot; (3pts), which is basically a Wraith that is well disposed towards the Vampire in question and helps them out. Mainly by offering advice and guidance, but also just being a person the Vampire can talk to who's not involved with the Jyhad. and the Flaw is Haunted (3pts), which is having an angry Wraith follow you around and makes life difficult for you in some way\u200b \u200b\u200bboth a strong tie to the Wraiths like Necromancy<br /> Killed by a vampire probably falls under Violence for the purpose of Legion assignment. Or Happenstance if he stumbled on the vampire in a vulnerable moment and saw something he wasn't supposed to see. One must uphold the masquerade after all.... Despair if you were a Blood Doll, and lost everything, only the Kiss remained. Mystery, after all... someone were just kissing your neck and have a greatest extasy in your life and... woke up as a Wraith. Whats happened? Fate? There must have been some reason, some purpose that led you to that exactly vampire who ate you...<br /> So even killed as a Vampire is not necesarry the source of ressentment<br /> Sure, Necromancy is a pain in the ghostly rear but even the victim of such power realises, most of the vampires are not familiar it.<br /> I highly doubt there is an universal hate toward the Vampires from the Wraith part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-19-2023, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T02:04:00-07:00","id":1518302,"title":"","content":"A tricky aspect of all this is that out of all the splats, only vampires have humanity mechanics, whereas all the others have no such restriction. This is kind of like the 40K Eldar calling humans barbarians, but overlooking the fact it was their own hedonism which created the Eye of Terror and gave birth to the chaos god Slannesh. <br /> <br /> More importantly though, given how relatively small the vampire population is, it is strange that the other splats have a generic response to vampires. It would make more sense that they would simply declare a given city or region off limits due to it being the home of vampires and staying away.<br /> <br /> But once Mage gets brought into this, it is canon that mages can cure vampirism regardless of Generation. So why exactly mages haven't used magical sensor sweeps to locate and then clear cities one by one is never addressed in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T04:00:47-07:00","id":1518303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518290#post1518290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are pretty hated by everything and everyone</div> </div> </div> </div>Because at the end of the day the existence of the Vampires in the World doesn't make it better in any way. It just makes it worse.<br /> For all their faults, the Mages seek a better world, the Fera seek to stop the destruction of the World and the Fae are the last bastions of Wonder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518290#post1518290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember, it's usually done for ghouling specific targets or blood bonding other vampires. No one is going around trying to make it a large scale practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cocaine is just sold to a specific population, no one is going around making it a large scale practice.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 07-19-2023, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T04:19:54-07:00","id":1518304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518293#post1518293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fera: Apparently they smell the Wyrm and because they are dead they that still &quot;alive&quot; apparently they have a connection with it, and we that know of the lore know this isn't true,.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't smell of the Wyrm because they are dead or because they are vampires. They smell of the Wyrm because of what they do. Vampires are parasites that prey upon humans and exploit them to perpetuate an increasingly alien existence that's based upon asserting dominance over everyone to hide the fact that you've got nothing else to exist for. The moral and philosophical lows they are willing to stoop to is what makes them tainted by the Wyrm. That's also the reason Vampires who really, really work hard on keeping their humanity high don't register - Vampires of high humanity aren't as destructive to everything around them as other Vampires. However, Vampires keeping high humanity is not likely. Even leaving the beast aside, if they want to interact with vampiric society they will do horrible things that will keep eroding their humanity.<br /> <br /> And they do have a connection with the Eater of Souls - who gave them their endless hunter and the Beast of War - who gave them their Beast They acquire their taint by willingly indulging the Defiler Wyrm. We do know that (in Werewolf at least).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T06:37:14-07:00","id":1518306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518278#post1518278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really the doing of the other games. V:tM set down the setting element of &quot;lupines kill vampires who try to go out into the wilderness&quot; back in the first green marble book, and everything just followed from there. The setting details of, say, W:tA only flesh out the Vampire-specified setting element (that being that Kindred act like BSDs, which no one wants to be around due with ill spiritual shit that follows them around a compounded issue, so Garou and Fera avoid them most times and end them when possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is true that both games did a lot from the start to set up an antagonistic relationship between vampires and werewolves, the details are more complicated. On my recent read-through of the original 1992 <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> core book, it amused me that the very first item in the appendix is a list of ten ways to do vampire-werewolf crossover chronicles -- including even a Romeo and Juliet type scenario where a Gangrel and a Garou fall in love!<br /> <br /> Earlier in the book, not buried in an appendix but right there in the main storytelling section of the game, there is this astonishing paragraph:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]ecause of the tremendous power the Kindred do have in mortal society, some Garou feel that Vampires are among the best hope for a quick solution to the current emergencies. In this type of Chronicle, you can essentially tell stories similar to the ones explained in <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> and the supplements for that game. Garou can work to end the intrigue and power games between certain Kindred in order to create an opportunity to gain the trust and assistance of important and powerful Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in its early stages, the World of Darkness seemed to be quite amenable to crossovers, but that element was downplayed heavily after around 1994-1995, when all of the original writers and developers had either left the company or were on their way out.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 07-19-2023, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T07:00:40-07:00","id":1518307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518306#post1518306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, in its early stages, the World of Darkness seemed to be quite amenable to crossovers, but that element was downplayed heavily after around 1994-1995, when all of the original writers and developers had either left the company or were on their way out.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>A legacy I tried to carry on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> WoD is much more fun if you fill your chronicles with everything and the kitchen sink <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T09:05:12-07:00","id":1518313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518303#post1518303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cocaine is just sold to a specific population, no one is going around making it a large scale practice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like cartels and other criminal organization are kinda trying to do that, or something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T11:38:10-07:00","id":1518317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518290#post1518290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I remember, it's usually done for ghouling specific targets or blood bonding other vampires. No one is going around trying to make it a large scale practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>As always, there needs to be a definition of what we're calling a &quot;large scale practice&quot; or a &quot;specific target.&quot;<br /> <br /> But one example that I feel certainly complicates that notion is a fellow named <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hedeon_Yaroslavich?so=search\" target=\"_blank\">Hedeon Yaroslavich</a>. He's admittedly from some earlier content, so there might be debates about whether or not this particular tactic would work, depending on edition:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The villages near his castle are populated to capacity with ghouls who drink from vitae-tainted wells, thereby becoming Blood Bound to Yaroslavich.\u200b </div> </div> </div>There's room for semantic debate, but I think one vampire using his Vitae to brainwash several villages worth of people goes beyond the typical scope of a term like &quot;specific target.&quot;<br /> <br /> And as people have pointed out, *this* is the kind of Vampire behaviour that, metaphorically speaking, &quot;makes headlines&quot;; a Golconda hermit who subsists entirely on squirrel blood probably doesn't meet too many other supernaturals, and those that do meet said Vampire probably aren't going to count as much more than hearsay when it comes to determining the collective impression of Vampires in their community.<br /> <br /> The hate is a little exaggerated, but it's not unreasonable. Other Splat absolutely do horrible things, but (again, as others have pointed out) they are generally able to justify it within their own perspectives, as a &quot;greater good/lesser evil&quot; kind of thing if nothing else, whereas most of the terrible stuff that Vampires do to people are just bread-and-butter parts of the conditions necessary for them to exist. Werewolves and Mages are significantly hampered if they make respecting the autonomy and well-being of others a priority when they pursue their goals; Vampires are almost fundamentally incapable of existing without abusing the physical and psychological well-being of others. Werewolves kind of come close with just how much horrible stuff is a consequence of their Rage, but Vampires don't really have the excuse of fighting a forever-war against the End of the World to defend themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T12:20:07-07:00","id":1518320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518317#post1518317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Werewolves kind of come close with just how much horrible stuff is a consequence of their Rage, but Vampires don't really have the excuse of fighting a forever-war against the End of the World to defend themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage isn't what prompted them to take the tack that they were &quot;the most chosen of Gaia&quot; and kill their fellows the first time. That was purely a sense of self-importance and utilitarianism that was on par with the Technocracy. Rage at least blows up and eases its hold from time to time; the cultural need to keep justifying their ancestors, meanwhile, has caused a perpetual and deadly lack of criticism toward their own ways at all times, lest they besmirch the Honor of their ancestors (which, as it has to be noted, are capable of manifesting to argue with them in caerns, and even possessing their descendants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T13:08:39-07:00","id":1518322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518320#post1518320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage isn't what prompted them to take the tack that they were &quot;the most chosen of Gaia&quot; and kill their fellows the first time. That was purely a sense of self-importance and utilitarianism that was on par with the Technocracy. Rage at least blows up and eases its hold from time to time; the cultural need to keep justifying their ancestors, meanwhile, has caused a perpetual and deadly lack of criticism toward their own ways at all times, lest they besmirch the Honor of their ancestors (which, as it has to be noted, are capable of manifesting to argue with them in caerns, and even possessing their descendants).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point, for sure! But I'm more speaking specifically about &quot;what innate characteristic of Werewolf existence makes them an intrinsic threat comparable to Vampires,&quot; and Rage is the closest answer that comes to mind.<br /> <br /> I'm also not trying to argue for the Garou perspective as correct, but rather the role it plays in justifying the evils of their existence, both to themselves and (hypothetically) to other Splats. Which plays into why Vampires have an especially hard time getting other Splats to take a live-and-let-live attitude, as the evil that comes with their existence is largely self-serving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T14:22:17-07:00","id":1518323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518322#post1518322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a fair point, for sure! But I'm more speaking specifically about &quot;what innate characteristic of Werewolf existence makes them an intrinsic threat comparable to Vampires,&quot; and Rage is the closest answer that comes to mind.<br /> <br /> I'm also not trying to argue for the Garou perspective as correct, but rather the role it plays in justifying the evils of their existence, both to themselves and (hypothetically) to other Splats. Which plays into why Vampires have an especially hard time getting other Splats to take a live-and-let-live attitude, as the evil that comes with their existence is largely self-serving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage, or combat forms gratis for all Garou? Because everyone having Celerity for a steep discount is surely daunting, but Crinos and Hispo surely make it existentially horrifying.<br /> <br /> (Ananasi blood shenanigans would probably freak the Kindred out more if they knew the full extent of the spiders' capabilities in that arena.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T16:07:31-07:00","id":1518331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518323#post1518323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rage, or combat forms gratis for all Garou? Because everyone having Celerity for a steep discount is surely daunting, but Crinos and Hispo surely make it existentially horrifying.<br /> <br /> (Ananasi blood shenanigans would probably freak the Kindred out more if they knew the full extent of the spiders' capabilities in that arena.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, this is still a misunderstanding. I'm not talking about the combat viability of each.<br /> <br /> I am talking about the threat that each Splat poses to Ordinary People, just trying to live their lives. And more importantly, How and Why they pose a threat. I'm talking about a comparison between the Beast and Rage as something that makes the members of the Splat threatening or downright dangerous to regular human beings who have not done anything to provoke a supernatural monster to come into their life and upend it, but might have it happen regardless.<br /> <br /> The OP has argued that prejudice against Vampires is excessive because the various criticisms that are directed at Vampires can be pointed at other Splats as well. The point I, and others, have been trying to make is that even if other Splats do cause as much harm to regular humans as Vampires do, there are factors that make it easier for them to avoid the criticisms directed at the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Firstly, harming regular people is more a choice that can be made or avoided by Mages and Werewolves, but is almost impossible for a Vampire as predation against humans is a necessary part of their unlives; the amount of effort a Vampire requires simply to avoid inflicting harm or psychological manipulation on regular humans as a necessary byproduct of their existence requires a lifestyle comparable to a normal human becoming an ascetic hermit.<br /> <br /> Secondly, many Mages and Werewolves that do inflict harm on regular humans often have a &quot;Big Picture&quot; argument that morally justifies it from their perspective. I'd say that the number of Vampires who see themselves as fighting an existential battle for the fate of the world, thereby justifying the evils of their continued existence, are probably in the minority. And the ones that are in that minority are going to include groups like the Sabbat, who aren't going to sell that argument very well.<br /> <br /> All that said and done, it's worth noting that a majority of Garou probably hate Mages only a tiny bit less than Vampires. And Mages don't so much hate Vampires as mistrust them. Again, it's a bit of an exaggeration to say they're the collective punching-bag of the setting. They're just kind of to the wider setting what the Setites are to Vampire society; implicitly untrustworthy and dangerous, even if sometimes you find yourself really needing something they have to offer and might need to deal with them on some level. Just make sure to triple-check it from every angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T18:17:25-07:00","id":1518338,"title":"","content":"Vampires eat humans, and most supernatural species have at least some humans that they like. Which is why most vampires also hate other vampires. That Brujah who genuinely likes humans in the anarchist/communist/libertarian/Nazi movement hates the vampires who eat them. That Ventrue who genuinely likes humans with old money family names and etiquette hates the vampires who eat them. Which at least sometimes means they hate themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T13:41:24-07:00","id":1518374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518306#post1518306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, in its early stages, the World of Darkness seemed to be quite amenable to crossovers, but that element was downplayed heavily after around 1994-1995, when all of the original writers and developers had either left the company or were on their way out.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. In the first few years of the game, the Developers clearly meant everything to be able to crossover and they encouraged it. However, some of the early crossovers were not done very well. They subverted the expectations of each individual game line, and created a different feel as a whole than what people wanted for a game that was based on classic supernatural monsters. So there was a pushback from the fan base, and I think that lead to a walk back from crossover that was later cemented very hard in Revised.<br /> <br /> I think one reason this happened is that players took the Litany far more seriously than they ever did the Traditions. The original description of the Garou showed a people in the beginning of a cultural collapse. Younger Garou were challenging the Litany, and too many elder Garou were hidebound and out of touch. There may not have been a War of Ages like in Vampire, but there was certainly generational (and lots of other) conflict. I suspect the Developers originally believed that the players would adopt a more pragmatic and self-interested approach to the Litany, and that there would be more openness to things like Garou and Gangrel working together. Or Shadow Lords working with Giovanni in the underworld. Or Bone Gnawers cooperating with the Sabbat (!) against mutual enemies.<br /> <br /> But players did not play like that. They ended up taking the Litany very seriously. And STs ran the elders as better leaders as well. (As an example, I've never seen STs roleplay Silver Fang NPCs as being poor leaders that are causing other tribes to consider removing them from the leadership.) So PCs didn't make exceptions for things like having allies or friends with vampires. And STs did not either. So the idea that a crossover style chronicle (not even meaning PCs are from the two groups, but simply that vampire NPCs could have a real role in Werewolf chronicles other than an enemy to be killed) quickly died. I know it does happen in some chronicles, but that is very much the exception.<br /> <br /> I think one reason (but not the only one) is that by tying in the Litany so heavily with Renown (especially Honor), it created a strong incentive to obey the Litany. Players hate losing XP. And Renown is simply another kind of XP earned in play. Why risk losing that hard earned Renown by making exceptions for this or that vampire? So the game in actual play turned over very different than how the setting was originally portrayed.<br /> <br /> However, since I always preferred the early description of the setting than the latter description, there is some appeal to me of some level of crossover between vampires and Garou... provided it makes sense. It shouldn't be normalized. But some Garou (concentrated more in certain tribes and camps than others) should have some secret connections. They just need to keep them secret.<br /> <br /> And I like the idea that in some capacity, a smart Gangrel who doesn't create trouble can somehow find ways to &quot;run with the wolves&quot; in some capacity. The problem is figuring out reasonable ways this can happen without making the Garou to be total idiots or just not give a crap about this Wyrm minion.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of things, I often feel that if the Developers had written their products to provide more concrete examples, things might have turned out differently. If they had include an occasional Lupine NPC in a By Night book, or a Leech NPC in a Rage book that portrayed some of these (crossover not intended to be enemies) examples in a way that added to that game line's feel rather than distracting it, things might have turned out differently.<br /> <br /> What would have happened if there was a vampire NPC shown in Rage Across New York that would have made a good ally against the Seventh Generation? Say by someone who would be useful against Van Gelding? Or a Garou NPC and Gangrel NPC who were in a Romeo &amp; Juliet situation (perhaps because they were lovers before either became the supernatural creature)? Or a Lupine of the tribe of Thunder who operated as an assassin of Kindred in Dark Colony who would work for multiple Kindred in order to gain sufficient boons to accomplish a goal? Honestly discuss the difficulty of such characters in these situations, but provide legitimate reasons they have been overcome.<br /> <br /> I think this topic deserves its own thread in either game forum, but I don't want to hijack this one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:10:53-07:00","id":1518377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518374#post1518374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this topic deserves its own thread in either game forum, but I don't want to hijack this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> That would be an excellent thread\u200b <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> be great if you could kick it off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:17:30-07:00","id":1518379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518374#post1518374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. In the first few years of the game, the Developers clearly meant everything to be able to crossover and they encouraged it. However, some of the early crossovers were not done very well. They subverted the expectations of each individual game line, and created a different feel as a whole than what people wanted for a game that was based on classic supernatural monsters. So there was a pushback from the fan base, and I think that lead to a walk back from crossover that was later cemented very hard in Revised.<br /> <br /> I think one reason this happened is that players took the Litany far more seriously than they ever did the Traditions. The original description of the Garou showed a people in the beginning of a cultural collapse. Younger Garou were challenging the Litany, and too many elder Garou were hidebound and out of touch. There may not have been a War of Ages like in Vampire, but there was certainly generational (and lots of other) conflict. I suspect the Developers originally believed that the players would adopt a more pragmatic and self-interested approach to the Litany, and that there would be more openness to things like Garou and Gangrel working together. Or Shadow Lords working with Giovanni in the underworld. Or Bone Gnawers cooperating with the Sabbat (!) against mutual enemies.<br /> <br /> But players did not play like that. They ended up taking the Litany very seriously. And STs ran the elders as better leaders as well. (As an example, I've never seen STs roleplay Silver Fang NPCs as being poor leaders that are causing other tribes to consider removing them from the leadership.) So PCs didn't make exceptions for things like having allies or friends with vampires. And STs did not either. So the idea that a crossover style chronicle (not even meaning PCs are from the two groups, but simply that vampire NPCs could have a real role in Werewolf chronicles other than an enemy to be killed) quickly died. I know it does happen in some chronicles, but that is very much the exception.<br /> <br /> I think one reason (but not the only one) is that by tying in the Litany so heavily with Renown (especially Honor), it created a strong incentive to obey the Litany. Players hate losing XP. And Renown is simply another kind of XP earned in play. Why risk losing that hard earned Renown by making exceptions for this or that vampire? So the game in actual play turned over very different than how the setting was originally portrayed.<br /> <br /> However, since I always preferred the early description of the setting than the latter description, there is some appeal to me of some level of crossover between vampires and Garou... provided it makes sense. It shouldn't be normalized. But some Garou (concentrated more in certain tribes and camps than others) should have some secret connections. They just need to keep them secret.<br /> <br /> And I like the idea that in some capacity, a smart Gangrel who doesn't create trouble can somehow find ways to &quot;run with the wolves&quot; in some capacity. The problem is figuring out reasonable ways this can happen without making the Garou to be total idiots or just not give a crap about this Wyrm minion.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of things, I often feel that if the Developers had written their products to provide more concrete examples, things might have turned out differently. If they had include an occasional Lupine NPC in a By Night book, or a Leech NPC in a Rage book that portrayed some of these (crossover not intended to be enemies) examples in a way that added to that game line's feel rather than distracting it, things might have turned out differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as the Garou were portrayed as stricter in adhering to the Litany, do you suppose that the Kindred NPCs in By Night books also complicated things in their presentations, out of curiosity? I personally haven't managed to get too many By Night books, so I can't really judge. Also, W:tA had that Rage CCG tie-in of NPCs, and the only vampire was... Vlad Rustovitch, a clear antagonist that hates Garou in general and Shadow Lords in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would have happened if there was a vampire NPC shown in Rage Across New York that would have made a good ally against the Seventh Generation? Say by someone who would be useful against Van Gelding? </div> </div> </div>I have to wonder how amenable Vampire players would have been to the reverse, with Garou showing up as obvious potential countermeasures to presented threats. Especially in the Cam vs. Sabbat struggle, since shovelheads and even vozhd tend to be rather low-level threats to werewolves, often falling behind dedicated combat fomori like gorehounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or a Garou NPC and Gangrel NPC who were in a Romeo &amp; Juliet situation (perhaps because they were lovers before either became the supernatural creature)? </div> </div> </div>Impossible without the Garou being a Skin Dancer, since Garou are born Garou. Knowing a Garou before their First Change is also kind of dangerous, as the change tends to result in casualties, but that might be why the vampire half of the relationship got embraced in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or a Lupine of the tribe of Thunder who operated as an assassin of Kindred in Dark Colony who would work for multiple Kindred in order to gain sufficient boons to accomplish a goal? Honestly discuss the difficulty of such characters in these situations, but provide legitimate reasons they have been overcome.<br /> <br /> I think this topic deserves its own thread in either game forum, but I don't want to hijack this one.<br /> </div> </div> </div>The first Shadow Lords book kind of put a nail into that before it could even be considered, with all of the Shadow Lords who had supported Dracula against other vampires ending up very, very dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T15:50:53-07:00","id":1518387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518374#post1518374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one reason this happened is that players took the Litany far more seriously than they ever did the Traditions. The original description of the Garou showed a people in the beginning of a cultural collapse. Younger Garou were challenging the Litany, and too many elder Garou were hidebound and out of touch. There may not have been a War of Ages like in Vampire, but there was certainly generational (and lots of other) conflict. I suspect the Developers originally believed that the players would adopt a more pragmatic and self-interested approach to the Litany, and that there would be more openness to things like Garou and Gangrel working together. Or Shadow Lords working with Giovanni in the underworld. Or Bone Gnawers cooperating with the Sabbat (!) against mutual enemies.<br /> <br /> But players did not play like that. They ended up taking the Litany very seriously. And STs ran the elders as better leaders as well. (As an example, I've never seen STs roleplay Silver Fang NPCs as being poor leaders that are causing other tribes to consider removing them from the leadership.) So PCs didn't make exceptions for things like having allies or friends with vampires. And STs did not either. So the idea that a crossover style chronicle (not even meaning PCs are from the two groups, but simply that vampire NPCs could have a real role in Werewolf chronicles other than an enemy to be killed) quickly died. I know it does happen in some chronicles, but that is very much the exception.<br /> <br /> I think one reason (but not the only one) is that by tying in the Litany so heavily with Renown (especially Honor), it created a strong incentive to obey the Litany. Players hate losing XP. And Renown is simply another kind of XP earned in play. Why risk losing that hard earned Renown by making exceptions for this or that vampire? So the game in actual play turned over very different than how the setting was originally portrayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these two things are intricately linked into a feedback loop. Players adhere to the litany motivated by wanting to be high in rank. Nominally most of the behaviors that are awarded renown are actually positive behaviours, the renown charts have very few rewarded negative behaviours. This leads to the fact that Garou in function end up more of a meritocracy than the leadership of the oldest and most powerful. They are powerful because they are good at what they do, and we will be powerful the same way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T16:15:18-07:00","id":1518390,"title":"","content":"Ultimately &quot;werewolf&quot; is the game that has the most Dungeons and Dragons influence, and that causes a lot of rigid play. You can clearly see the influence of the Druid, Barbarian, and Paladin classes in various design choices and mechanics. Since you advance like a Paladin obsessing about his oath, you really aren't incentivized to play as anything other than Taliban type religious fanatic. If they wanted more nuanced play, they really should have studied incentive structures more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T16:56:45-07:00","id":1518391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518390#post1518390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ultimately &quot;werewolf&quot; is the game that has the most Dungeons and Dragons influence, and that causes a lot of rigid play. You can clearly see the influence of the Druid, Barbarian, and Paladin classes in various design choices and mechanics. Since you advance like a Paladin obsessing about his oath, you really aren't incentivized to play as anything other than Taliban type religious fanatic. If they wanted more nuanced play, they really should have studied incentive structures more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole WtA is kinda like D&amp;D is a very weird interpretation that doesn't hold up under any deeper scrutiny. Werewolf is not where the only systems exist to resolve combat encounters and where the main impetus of the game is killing monsters and collecting loot to go to the next better place for killing monsters and collecting loot.<br /> <br /> There's loads of nuanced play in Werewolf. They actually care about ideas, people and things. The game itself is incredibly political and about getting people to do what you need them to do, or figuring out how to do your duty and do what you need to do for yourself (and which shortcuts are you willing to take).<br /> <br /> Just because they don't like Vampires doesn't mean they lack nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T21:01:20-07:00","id":1518409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518391#post1518391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's loads of nuanced play in Werewolf. </div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest Werewolf is more Vampire than Vampire <i>itself</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T23:04:09-07:00","id":1518414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518390#post1518390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ultimately &quot;werewolf&quot; is the game that has the most Dungeons and Dragons influence, and that causes a lot of rigid play. You can clearly see the influence of the Druid, Barbarian, and Paladin classes in various design choices and mechanics. Since you advance like a Paladin obsessing about his oath, you really aren't incentivized to play as anything other than Taliban type religious fanatic. If they wanted more nuanced play, they really should have studied incentive structures more.</div> </div> </div> </div>You advance by getting deeds <i>recognized</i>, which is an important specification. In addition to things that actually happened, you can lie about what you've done to get ahead. There are some pretty terrible consequences for failing to keep things under wraps, and fooling the spirits that uphold the system is difficult, but if the Apocalypse is coming, it's on the table. After all, it could mean the difference between having no defense against silver and being able to not just soak it as long as the moon is out, but also ensure that it turns on its wielder during the full moon. Finally, bribery is also possible, but the game doesn't tend to discuss it in concrete terms, and it tends to put a lot of stress on the pact that the various established societies have with spirits.<br /> <br /> But in the arena of actually doing what you get credit for, not only do Honor and Wisdom exist, Glory can also be had for, not counting just killing enemies...<br /> <br /> Traveling to umbral realms and coming back alive<br /> Putting yourself in danger for others and getting injured<br /> Celebrating said wounds<br /> Participating in a Great Hunt<br /> Doing necessary scutwork for your sept and/or tribe<br /> Serving a position in a sept, even a non-combat one<br /> Justly challenging another Garou<br /> Telling really good stories<br /> <br /> So sharpen up that Expression Ability, because it's time to go get both Glory and Wisdom <b>at the same time!</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also, paladins didn't get xp for following their oath in 1e. They had to bring treasure up from the dungeon like everyone else, preferably as valuable as possible for the smallest unit of weight (just like everyone else, gp was xp)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T23:29:42-07:00","id":1518415,"title":"","content":"Obsessing over a Paladins oath was also survival method since if you violated the oath, you lost all magical powers and permanently became a basic fighter, at least in the early editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T23:39:18-07:00","id":1518416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird#post1518277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, feels kind of weird.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I thin you're getting that feeling because there's a bunch of mixed messages going on in the writing for the game, as other people have explained above. The lore and the rules have been written by a bunch of different people, with a bunch of different agendas, and interpreted by a whole load more people with a whole load more agendas.<br /> <br /> The crucial thing to remember, to my mind at least, is Rule Zero. This is an RPG and the rules and lore are there to provide inspiration for _your_ game. You are not required to follow the lore or the rules at any point. There's no RPG inquisition checking that you've memorised a hundred odd books and are sticking to every rule and contradiction within them. It's meant to be fun so go ahead and play the game you want, if something in the rules or the lore doesn't make sense, or even flatly opposes your concept, then all you have to do is make sure the other players around the table are informed adn agreeable.<br /> <br /> Strict adherence to every word in every book will soon have you spinning in circles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T02:55:39-07:00","id":1518420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518391#post1518391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole WtA is kinda like D&amp;D is a very weird interpretation that doesn't hold up under any deeper scrutiny. Werewolf is not where the only systems exist to resolve combat encounters and where the main impetus of the game is killing monsters and collecting loot to go to the next better place for killing monsters and collecting loot.<br /> <br /> There's loads of nuanced play in Werewolf. They actually care about ideas, people and things. The game itself is incredibly political and about getting people to do what you need them to do, or figuring out how to do your duty and do what you need to do for yourself (and which shortcuts are you willing to take).</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever the topic of Dungeons &amp; Dragons comes up on these forums (and in the wider World of Darkness fandom in general), I regularly marvel at how outlandish the characterizations of the game appear to me. I should probably stop responding to all the D&amp;D tangents that crop up, because it has resulted in painful exchanges many times in the past, but...<br /> <br /> How is this in any way a charitable description of D&amp;D? In my experience, this is a version of the game that only exists in the detractors' heads. &quot;The only systems exist to resolve combat encounters&quot; does not accurately describe the original 1974 Dungeons &amp; Dragons release (where the entirety of the combat rules fit into maybe a couple of pages, and the game is just as interested in castle construction, the establishment and maintenance of baronies, aerial and naval movement, and so on); it does not describe either version of Advanced Dungeons &amp; Dragons (which only expand in a dizzying variety on the social and exploration systems already present in OD&amp;D); and it does not describe any of the Wizards of the Coast editions of the game (each of which has a detailed skill system for interacting with the imaginary world in non-combat capacity).<br /> <br /> In the 20+ years that I have played or run Dungeons &amp; Dragons, characters have always cared about ideas, people, and things, and the games have always been very nuanced and highly political. Maybe these archetypal &quot;kill monsters and collect loot to kill more monsters and collect more loot&quot; games really do exist. If that's how a group wants to engage with the game, more power to them. I would strongly argue that it says more about the group than the game -- the bunch of 13-year-olds who do the hack-and-slash routine every Thursday night are not going to turn into a mature and sophisticated ensemble of Real Storytelling just because the game changes from D&amp;D to <i>Werewolf.</i>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 07-21-2023, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T03:44:24-07:00","id":1518421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518298#post1518298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Wraith </b>are... they know. But hate? I wouldn't say that.<br /> Some of them are wraith because a feeding went wrong and/or a Vampire lost it and a killing spree<br /> Vampire have a bit more interaction with a Wraith.<br /> The Merit is &quot;Spirit Mentor&quot; (3pts), which is basically a Wraith that is well disposed towards the Vampire in question and helps them out. Mainly by offering advice and guidance, but also just being a person the Vampire can talk to who's not involved with the Jyhad. and the Flaw is Haunted (3pts), which is having an angry Wraith follow you around and makes life difficult for you in some way\u200b \u200b\u200bboth a strong tie to the Wraiths like Necromancy<br /> Killed by a vampire probably falls under Violence for the purpose of Legion assignment. Or Happenstance if he stumbled on the vampire in a vulnerable moment and saw something he wasn't supposed to see. One must uphold the masquerade after all.... Despair if you were a Blood Doll, and lost everything, only the Kiss remained. Mystery, after all... someone were just kissing your neck and have a greatest extasy in your life and... woke up as a Wraith. Whats happened? Fate? There must have been some reason, some purpose that led you to that exactly vampire who ate you...<br /> So even killed as a Vampire is not necesarry the source of ressentment<br /> Sure, Necromancy is a pain in the ghostly rear but even the victim of such power realises, most of the vampires are not familiar it.<br /> I highly doubt there is an universal hate toward the Vampires from the Wraith part</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore, among the Wraiths, there are Puppeteers and Risen who are deeply involved in vampire politics. They hold a high regard for the Camarilla and its adherence to the Masquerade, as it greatly aids Renegades in evading detection by Stygia. These Wraiths actively assimilate into the vampire society, capable of coexisting due to their shared disciplines, similar unlifestyles, and distinct sources of sustenance.<br /> <br /> And there is/was the case of the First City in the Shadowlands, where vampires, Idran Awakened Mages, ghosts and (some unlucky and deranged) werewolves live as a happy family. The Tal'Mahe'Ra book says &quot;the vast majority of ghosts would jump at the chance to live under the protection of Enoch outside of the Hierarchy's reach&quot;, so wraith-vampire relationships are rather wholesome for the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28102-stathmin","name":"Stathmin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T12:03:54-07:00","id":1518440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518415#post1518415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsessing over a Paladins oath was also survival method since if you violated the oath, you lost all magical powers and permanently became a basic fighter, at least in the early editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, Lawful Good was apparently very... permissive of things that most people wouldn't consider either lawful or good in any way, shape or form, according to Gary Gygax in a rather &quot;what the hell&quot; post praising one Colonel John Milton Chivington of Sand Creek Massacre infamy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T14:26:49-07:00","id":1518452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518420#post1518420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whenever the topic of Dungeons &amp; Dragons comes up on these forums (and in the wider World of Darkness fandom in general), I regularly marvel at how outlandish the characterizations of the game appear to me. I should probably stop responding to all the D&amp;D tangents that crop up, because it has resulted in painful exchanges many times in the past, but...<br /> <br /> How is this in any way a charitable description of D&amp;D? In my experience, this is a version of the game that only exists in the detractors' heads. &quot;The only systems exist to resolve combat encounters&quot; does not accurately describe the original 1974 Dungeons &amp; Dragons release (where the entirety of the combat rules fit into maybe a couple of pages, and the game is just as interested in castle construction, the establishment and maintenance of baronies, aerial and naval movement, and so on); it does not describe either version of Advanced Dungeons &amp; Dragons (which only expand in a dizzying variety on the social and exploration systems already present in OD&amp;D); and it does not describe any of the Wizards of the Coast editions of the game (each of which has a detailed skill system for interacting with the imaginary world in non-combat capacity).<br /> <br /> In the 20+ years that I have played or run Dungeons &amp; Dragons, characters have always cared about ideas, people, and things, and the games have always been very nuanced and highly political. Maybe these archetypal &quot;kill monsters and collect loot to kill more monsters and collect more loot&quot; games really do exist. If that's how a group wants to engage with the game, more power to them. I would strongly argue that it says more about the group than the game -- the bunch of 13-year-olds who do the hack-and-slash routine every Thursday night are not going to turn into a mature and sophisticated ensemble of Real Storytelling just because the game changes from D&amp;D to <i>Werewolf.</i>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to step back here and look at the bigger picture. D&amp;D as a system has a core loop of kill monsters - level up. Through the ages they have done a lot of changes and softening things up, but it's still a system where every character type exists of practically only combat abilities, and even the skill monkies like rogues and bards have a problem with the swinginess of the system. You can ignore this game loop and these abilities (and the way you gain them back in the modern day) but you're essentially ignoring most of what D&amp;D is designed to be.<br /> <br /> Now, that doesn't mean that you cannot play D&amp;D in a mature and dramatic way that will be better than any high drama modern narrative game, but you'll be doing that by ignoring and bending the core premise and core tools of the system. I say this as someone who loves the settings and ideas in D&amp;D and has been giving it many chances through history (I even did a 40ish session of 5E Eberron campaign because I promised to and I gave up because I fought with the system too much to give the players the story they wanted and I wanted).<br /> <br /> When we speak of the baseline D&amp;D experience it's still - go to exotic places, kill strange people, become stronger, repeat. Even the modern adventures tend towards that, and recently they've been actually offering ideas of how to bypass &quot;encounters&quot; without combat as a novel thing in the mainline adventures. A shocking revalation and one that most people who moved away from D&amp;D have internalized a long time ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T03:46:26-07:00","id":1518511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stathmin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518421#post1518421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Furthermore, among the Wraiths, there are Puppeteers and Risen who are deeply involved in vampire politics. They hold a high regard for the Camarilla and its adherence to the Masquerade, as it greatly aids Renegades in evading detection by Stygia. These Wraiths actively assimilate into the vampire society, capable of coexisting due to their shared disciplines, similar unlifestyles, and distinct sources of sustenance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is realtively common for Wraiths - or at least common for some Wraiths in many and varied factions and belonging to all sorts of categories - to associate, befriend, cooperate, and share stories ; with Vampires from different Clans, Families, Guilds, and other types of groups.<br /> <br /> In many situations and under many circumstances it might be easy, valueable, and sensible for Ghosts and Kindred to interact and work together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T04:03:06-07:00","id":1518512,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it the dislike other groups have for vampires makes sense even on a personal level. Irl one of the easiest push backs against prejudice interacting with members of a group since our common humanity begins to sneak in. By contrast when you interact with a vampire it's typically a toxic dynamic so will re enforces your prejudices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T04:35:48-07:00","id":1518515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518511#post1518511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it is realtively common for Wraiths - or at least common for some Wraiths in many and varied factions and belonging to all sorts of categories - to associate, befriend, cooperate, and share stories ; with Vampires from different Clans, Families, Guilds, and other types of groups.<br /> <br /> In many situations and under many circumstances it might be easy, valueable, and sensible for Ghosts and Kindred to interact and work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense, of all the splats Wraiths are stating the obvious supernaturally enhanced dead humans, who aren't allowed to intract with the non-supernatural living, the next best thing is to interact with vampires who have their own codes of secrecy, just avoid the varieties who can control or even feed on them.<br /> They have a lot to gain from having supernatural allies who technically don't fall under the Dictum Mortum and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Many Wraiths once they've orientated to the shock of what the afterlife really is, are going to continue their human pursuits in a very hostile world (survival, power, treachery etc), there's a lot of resonance with the Kindred, after all vampire society is essentially an extreme pyramid of paranoid power games where each vampire attempts to continue their existance by accumulating influence and power to stay (un)alive, so are Wraiths to an extent being the other immortal race.<br /> <br /> Werewolves/Garou - I've never bought into the mindless killing machine motif that blindly obeys the Litany, yes there are exteme elements but for a race facing destruction simple survival of the fittest suggests they would rely on (or use) their human intelligence and be able to sensibly interpret the Litany to avoid every cub being destroyed within their first few months, since the first change.<br /> <br /> Canon also contradicts itself throughout versions by saying that all Kindred are tainted by the Wyrm, unless they have a Humanity over 7 but that the Garou have bigger more immediate wyrm opponents so live and let live, in reality yes the garou wouldn't like Kindred but by going on the above it suggests that some septs are a lot more pragmatic (if even to survive).<br /> Plus some tribes or septs may well work on th basis of the enemy of my enemy is my friend.<br /> <br /> Mage I think would avoid them because they are living humans, being in close proximity to a natural predator (for most people) is the same as a person being sat near a cobra ie they are going to be very uncomfortable waiting for the predator to strike, a Kindred with lower humanity or the beast close to the surface is giving off those warning signals.<br /> <br /> Aside from the prevading problem of Banality Changelings would either feel the same as humans and Mage or be unconcerned as they are powerful in their own right.<br /> Again whereabouts the coming Winter and Banality is a set-piece for CTD after some 800 years and a cycle of reincarnation its hard to imagine that Changelings haven't developed ways to endure banality even for short periods, which would suggest interaction between vampires and changelings (some clans and kiths more than others).<br /> <br /> After all how are the Unseelie happy to interact with the Sabbat who arguably are some of the most banal vampires.<br /> <br /> Kindred are toxic unnatural creatures so it makes sense that most living creatures who are aware of them give them a wide berth, but I think due to writer dislike of interaction or simple laziness broad assumptions were applied which are then contradicted by examples in canon, sort of writers writing themselves into a corner and then having to create a contradicting clause later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T10:53:26-07:00","id":1518648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518515#post1518515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolves/Garou - I've never bought into the mindless killing machine motif that blindly obeys the Litany, yes there are exteme elements but for a race facing destruction simple survival of the fittest suggests they would rely on (or use) their human intelligence and be able to sensibly interpret the Litany to avoid every cub being destroyed within their first few months, since the first change.<br /> <br /> Canon also contradicts itself throughout versions by saying that all Kindred are tainted by the Wyrm, unless they have a Humanity over 7 but that the Garou have bigger more immediate wyrm opponents so live and let live, in reality yes the garou wouldn't like Kindred but by going on the above it suggests that some septs are a lot more pragmatic (if even to survive).<br /> Plus some tribes or septs may well work on th basis of the enemy of my enemy is my friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires suffer extreme agony when a werewolf attempts to use rites to purify them of spiritual corruption. That usually only happens to beings that are flat out of the Wyrm, like fomori or banes, so it's not a good optic for Kindred, on the few occasions when everyone goes through with it and witnesses the results, and it doesn't rely on having a low Humanity, either. High Humanity only masks the presence of their inner corruption. Golconda might change that, but the certainty of this has been steadily eroded over the editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T12:34:15-07:00","id":1518655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518648#post1518648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires suffer extreme agony when a werewolf attempts to use rites to purify them of spiritual corruption. That usually only happens to beings that are flat out of the Wyrm, like fomori or banes, so it's not a good optic for Kindred, on the few occasions when everyone goes through with it and witnesses the results, and it doesn't rely on having a low Humanity, either. High Humanity only masks the presence of their inner corruption. Golconda might change that, but the certainty of this has been steadily eroded over the editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent point which is why other gifts pick them out as clearly horribly unnatural beings, even if you just stick to the Lupines of VTM the olfactory abilities of wolf forms is going to identify vampires pretty quickly (the lack of scent and pheromones for example).<br /> <br /> My main point is that given contradictions in canon, the Garous dislike for Kindred is probably more simple than they\u2019re just creatures of the Wyrm (as they seem to ignore the obvious Wyrm taint a lot), they are competition and rival predators that encroach on Garou interests &amp; territory and prey on kinfolk.<br /> <br /> If the more significant reason for conflict is purely territorial some Garou are more likely to begrudgingly tolerate and even work with Camarilla vampires (given their efforts to control predatory behaviour and maintain humanity so registering as less Wyrmish (even if it\u2019s a facade which I agree it is)).<br /> <br /> Looking at the inconsistencies, why attack Chicago and leave New York, Philadelphia or Montreal, the Paths of Enlightenment are a forsaking of Humanity so Sabbat strongholds would be right up their in terms of Wyrm taint and Hellholes, yet the Garou only target two Camarilla strongholds in Chicago and Milwaukee. (Because they\u2019ve apparently been manipulated rather than following the Litany).<br /> <br /> And in New York they go after the Seventh Generation and leave the Sabbat alone, whereabouts in New England the Garou actively target roaming packs - is it because the Garou aren\u2019t going after pure Wyrm taint but are destroying clearly monstrous creatures (Packs) encroaching on their territory which indicates interpretation of the Litany.<br /> <br /> So if we stick to interpreting these areas of canon (rather than conceding the real reason is writers are just keeping things separate and it being one of many many inconsistencies in WOD) it indicates the Garou are willing to tolerate Kindred despite the Litany.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T15:19:25-07:00","id":1518664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518655#post1518655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an excellent point which is why other gifts pick them out as clearly horribly unnatural beings, even if you just stick to the Lupines of VTM the olfactory abilities of wolf forms is going to identify vampires pretty quickly (the lack of scent and pheromones for example).<br /> <br /> My main point is that given contradictions in canon, the Garous dislike for Kindred is probably more simple than they\u2019re just creatures of the Wyrm (as they seem to ignore the obvious Wyrm taint a lot), they are competition and rival predators that encroach on Garou interests &amp; territory and prey on kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>We already covered that a bit of a ways upward with &quot;no one likes vampires, on account of what vampires do from night to night. Not even other vampires.&quot; However, you're glossing over some important nuances here.<br /> <br /> 1 - Garou are not just &quot;rival predators&quot;. If that were the case, their conflict could be avoided by simple niche partitioning. There's a clear cultural conflict that goes on between the two, and in the case of the Garou, that's defined largely by the bits of the litany that they still follow (everyone follows keeping the veil and guarding caerns assiduously, others tend to be up to interpretation).<br /> <br /> 2 - Vampires aren't actually competition. They aren't after the same things at the ground level or even floors above it, as vampires seek to prolong their downward spiral so that they can eventually be the centuries-old masters of intrigue. Garou, meanwhile, are after opportunities to prove themselves to the spirits, which are beings that Kindred largely don't even realize exist. You have really different priorities when you are or are not ageless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the more significant reason for conflict is purely territorial some Garou are more likely to begrudgingly tolerate and even work with Camarilla vampires (given their efforts to control predatory behaviour and maintain humanity so registering as less Wyrmish (even if it\u2019s a facade which I agree it is)).<br /> <br /> Looking at the inconsistencies, why attack Chicago and leave New York, Philadelphia or Montreal, the Paths of Enlightenment are a forsaking of Humanity so Sabbat strongholds would be right up their in terms of Wyrm taint and Hellholes, yet the Garou only target two Camarilla strongholds in Chicago and Milwaukee. (Because they\u2019ve apparently been manipulated rather than following the Litany). </div> </div> </div>Again, most vampires are really quite ignorant of spiritual matters, which extends to not having much active influence on the penumbra. This means that Sabbat territory isn't really more of a Hellhole risk than Cam territory. The Cam also willingly work with WICs when it benefits them, so there's no real reliance on saying that one sect is more manageable than the other. Plus, yeeting Sabbat packs that think that they've seen everything is a good way to get some quick Glory, perhaps even Wisdom from a novel approach to negating their advantages or hitting a really vulnerable center of operations, possible via devising a new Gift or rite. That Renown could be a tipping point in Rank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in New York they go after the Seventh Generation and leave the Sabbat alone, whereabouts in New England the Garou actively target roaming packs - is it because the Garou aren\u2019t going after pure Wyrm taint but are destroying clearly monstrous creatures (Packs) encroaching on their territory which indicates interpretation of the Litany.<br /> <br /> So if we stick to interpreting these areas of canon (rather than conceding the real reason is writers are just keeping things separate and it being one of many many inconsistencies in WOD) it indicates the Garou are willing to tolerate Kindred despite the Litany.\u200b </div> </div> </div>What it indicates is that there aren't enough Garou to go around, and they pick their battles with gritted teeth and much trepidation. The opportunity costs are terrible, but at the end of the day, you pay up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T23:28:55-07:00","id":1518683,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Vampire and Garou truces and even alliances occasionally happen<br /> During the aftermath of the War of Chicago in 1993, in which Lodin was destroyed (by either Kindred or Garou), Inyanga acted alone to negotiate a temporary and fragile peace accord with the Garou, though she presented herself to the Garou as the representative of the city's Kindred (she was portryed as a Gangrel, but is is more likely is the member of the Akunanse Legacy of the Laibon - this could be a factor with the whole Orun and Aye system, not to mention Inyanga, as a mortal, was a shaman who lived among the African nation that would later become the Zulus and was capable of shapeshifting and was well-versed in knowledge of the ways of the spirits... as a &quot;Human&quot;)<br /> In Vancouver, Prince Siegfried made a deal with the Garou, forming the Covenant. Siegfried would aid in reforestation and lobby against resource exploitation in the region, and the Garou would guard his domain from his enemies and refrain from unprovoked violence. Siegfried has fought against pentex on multiple occasions as well, dealing with wyrm corrupted mages on behalf of the Garou (okay, the Covenant fell a part due to various manipulations, but for quite a long time it worked and was benefical to both parties, especially the Garou)<br /> The Uktena in Louisiana established a treaty with the Camarilla of New Orleans after collectively fighting off the Black Spiral Dancers in the state<br /> <br /> While true, Chicago by Night is a 1991 supplement, (and the 2nd ed is '93), Dark Alliance: Vancouver is an 1993 one, New Orleans by Night is from 1994 so this could be part of the &quot;corssover-firendliness&quot; of the early materials, the facts remain these things happened<br /> <br /> The two city tribes deal with vampires as necessary, and often, lets say prioritize other targets above the leeches that make themselves useful. Glass Walkers often vie for their real estate and influence. Although not as influential as their vampiric rivals, Glass Walkers are wealthier than most other werewolves, and far more technically proficient.... Many Glass Walkers have positive relations with Ventrue and Toreador vampires, despite the Litany's prohibition against dealing with the Kindred. These more civilized Kindred see the Glass Walkers as perhaps the last hope of making peace with the Garou, although competition in financial spheres has also caused conflict in the past.<br /> As for the other tribes? Well the <i>expectation</i> is that vampires are to be killed, but individual Garou may have reasons for not doing so.<br /> There's no tribe that is officially cool with the Kindred but there are numerous exceptions to the &quot;kill on sight&quot; policy.<br /> <br /> And of course the whole thing boils down if you use Lupines or Garou?<br /> Lets use the Garou, aka. WtA version of Werewolves.<br /> And important thing is... Garou cannot instinctively sense Wyrm taint. There is a gift that must be learned to do so. <br /> More often than not, a Garou don't even know that Sense Wyrm and use it 0-24, nor too keen to use in the city; the Gift especially states &quot;Garou should remember that the Wyrm\u2019s taint can cling to relatively blameless souls. Werewolves may sense an innocent person who happens to work in a Wyrm-controlled factory or who has eated tainted food' - actually most of the time even fellow packmambers could be register because of some residue Taint that lingering around after that night in the city...<br /> There are more factors I think, namely a Garou's Rage and Primal Urge<br /> These two aspects of the character - IF we talk about how a charater woudl react to a vampire, but if just overall a Garou reaction my point still stands - are most likely to define the reaction to a walking corpse. Rage is instinctive, and a high Rage suggests they are more likely to use violence as a first resort. Primal Urge, on the other hand, represents their connection to the more animalistic portion of their heritage, and thereby likely give rise to instinctual responses of revulsion or disgust. So kids, don't bring your Ahroun to peace summits...<br /> A thrid part of this equation is the Garou's supernatural &quot;education&quot;. Packs and Spets are very different. Sept that is fully dedicated to matters that traditionally do not concern vampires (for example, a Sept that is more concerned with preserving an Umbral vantage, or that is engaged in a war with a non-vampiric foe) and maybe never even met, just heard stories about the spawns of the Bloody Man and will teaches the Cubs different things.<br /> If a Cub was raised in an urban and urbane Sept, (or they may have been raised in a system where such a treaty is already in place) they may have been educated on restraint in such a circumstance. To prioritize.<br /> Shadow Lords and Uktena both carry the stereotype of being willing to dirty their hands to get a job done. A traditional member of either tribe would put their intended objective ahead of something as pesky as what a potential ally's condition is. <br /> <br /> There are canon loopholes that will justify the Garou-Vampire cooperation. If you want to stay true to setting, those loopholes should be well thought out and well realized: the Glass Walkers realize the local Ventrue control the police, and no one is happy being constantly harassed by people whose disappearance will be noticed by the community. The Bone Gnawer needed that intel, and it's not like the Nosferatu was dumping sewage. The Uktena recognizes that parasites are part of Gaia's order, and what is a vampire if not a leech? And what secrets they might share!<br /> <br /> I say, it is quite an exaggeration the hate between the Garou and Cainites are universal<br /> At first glance and &quot;officially&quot; sure!<br /> But even if you scratch the surface just a tiny little bit, I think the reality is way different than the theory\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T01:00:49-07:00","id":1518687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518683#post1518683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Vampire and Garou truces and even alliances occasionally happen<br /> During the aftermath of the War of Chicago in 1993, in which Lodin was destroyed (by either Kindred or Garou), Inyanga acted alone to negotiate a temporary and fragile peace accord with the Garou, though she presented herself to the Garou as the representative of the city's Kindred (she was portryed as a Gangrel, but is is more likely is the member of the Akunanse Legacy of the Laibon - this could be a factor with the whole Orun and Aye system, not to mention Inyanga, as a mortal, was a shaman who lived among the African nation that would later become the Zulus and was capable of shapeshifting and was well-versed in knowledge of the ways of the spirits... as a &quot;Human&quot;)<br /> In Vancouver, Prince Siegfried made a deal with the Garou, forming the Covenant. Siegfried would aid in reforestation and lobby against resource exploitation in the region, and the Garou would guard his domain from his enemies and refrain from unprovoked violence. Siegfried has fought against pentex on multiple occasions as well, dealing with wyrm corrupted mages on behalf of the Garou (okay, the Covenant fell a part due to various manipulations, but for quite a long time it worked and was benefical to both parties, especially the Garou)<br /> The Uktena in Louisiana established a treaty with the Camarilla of New Orleans after collectively fighting off the Black Spiral Dancers in the state.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lets not forget the Uktena helping to protect and hide Menele after his battle with Helena.<br /> <br /> But thats my point I'm in agreement that there are nuances but there are also cultural differences between the tribes and Septs that dictate their approach, however as outlined above those nuances suggest that in the days of the Apocalypse\u200b that the Garou and kindred are not only prioritising greater threats but also recognising that non-aggression and sometimes alliances can be useful.<br /> <br /> As I said in my earlier post why would the the North East and East Coast Septs tolerate the Sabbat holding New York for so long, even with the Cardinals and Bishops clamping down on the more blatant excesses, you have several dozen vampires who are unwittingly furthering the wyrms presence and the sheer numbers of banes in th city would draw the Garous attention that some (if not a lot) of it is linked to the vampires presence.<br /> <br /> Especially when the Garou can compare intelligence and note that the Wyrms presence isn't necessarily strong in every city with a larger kindred population.<br /> <br /> Manhatten Island is a sacred place of Gaia and resists the taint, granted Pentax have major offices in New York, but the activities of the Sabbat are easily on a par with The Seventh Generation, a Sabbat Church or Rack could quickly become a taint.<br /> <br /> So even during the early 20th Century Urban Garou would be able to see that the vampires controlling New York are very wyrmish and their excesses directy supporting the defilers work.<br /> Granted Rage across New York indicates taht the local garou were hampered by their own in-fighting and then targeted the obvious Wyrm presence, but it suggests probably another alliance where some Garou factions aided the Camarilla in retaking the city (New York by Night written in a period when cross-overs are a straight no), and we don't know enough about Philadelphia other than it being a Sabbat city as to why the Garou haven't acted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518683#post1518683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say, it is quite an exaggeration the hate between the Garou and Cainites are universal<br /> At first glance and &quot;officially&quot; sure!<br /> But even if you scratch the surface just a tiny little bit, I think the reality is way different than the theory\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Which is as we said some tribes, camps or even Septs its a flat no (Egypt for example) if you take Milwaukee by Night into WTA clearly the local Septs view any Kindred as wyrm spawn to be mercilessly destroyed (that or theres some form of vendetta) but lack the numbers to raid the city and exterminate them, whilst others are indifferent and some see the merit in working together if it makes up for their reduced numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T01:12:45-07:00","id":1518688,"title":"","content":"Indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518687#post1518687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So even during the early 20th Century Urban Garou would be able to see that the vampires controlling New York are very wyrmish and their excesses directy supporting the defilers work.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a sprawling, ever-expanding Tzimisce Antediluvian beneath New York won't help the whole Wyrmish sense of New York either<br /> The Umbra must be horrendous around It - escpecially if its indeed &quot;alive&quot; and drains energy/life/sustenance from the very earth itself with is &quot;roots&quot;<br /> On the other hand... it is so alien at this point (and transcended it unliving larvar stage) it could be considered... a Wyld entity? <br /> (And have a connection to the Metamorphic Plague that &quot;torments&quot; the Black Furies...? The plague alters a fundamental principle within the person dramatically, i.e. turns a 180 degree arc on it. Personalities, memories, and even gender can change... this is very Dracon-like and the Dracon and the Furies shared territories)<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T05:29:05-07:00","id":1518695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518688#post1518688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well a sprawling, ever-expanding Tzimisce Antediluvian beneath New York won't help the whole Wyrmish sense of New York either<br /> The Umbra must be horrendous around It - escpecially if its indeed &quot;alive&quot; and drains energy/life/sustenance from the very earth itself with is &quot;roots&quot;<br /> On the other hand... it is so alien at this point (and transcended it unliving larvar stage) it could be considered... a Wyld entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>That presents an evil idea.....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> A bitter irony could be that the presence of the Gaian energy on Manhattan is actually the Tzimisce Antediluvian's Wyld signature or that the Wyld seeing it as a metamorphic creature of change has enshrouded it in Wyld energies, I can imagine investigating Garou would be pretty upset and confused to find Gorgons protecting something vampiric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T15:49:26-07:00","id":1518723,"title":"","content":"Re: Elder Brother hiding a vampire, that could work by the same rationale as binding away banes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518695#post1518695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That presents an evil idea.....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> A bitter irony could be that the presence of the Gaian energy on Manhattan is actually the Tzimisce Antediluvian's Wyld signature or that the Wyld seeing it as a metamorphic creature of change has enshrouded it in Wyld energies, I can imagine investigating Garou would be pretty upset and confused to find Gorgons protecting something vampiric.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld ain't Gaia. The Wyld only gets you more Wyld, and you'd know if it were around in large , because there would be Thresholds aplenty, with vortices spilling out of what had once been caerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T18:54:42-07:00","id":1518728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518695#post1518695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bitter irony could be that the presence of the Gaian energy on Manhattan is actually the Tzimisce Antediluvian's Wyld signature or that the Wyld seeing it as a metamorphic creature of change has enshrouded it in Wyld energies, I can imagine investigating Garou would be pretty upset and confused to find Gorgons protecting something vampiric.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm can also change and mutate things, and considering what the Cathedral of Flesh is, it's a vastly more likely patron than the Wyld.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T19:35:59-07:00","id":1518733,"title":"","content":"Depends on what the Wyrm IS, which is often contradictory. Sometimes the Wyrm is a very humanistic version of evil, which makes no sense in a world where male lions murder the children of rivals, and ducks constantly commit sexual assault, and are considered natural and of the Wyld. Sometimes it's all forces of decay, which means that everything from bacteria to vultures are of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T00:51:49-07:00","id":1518742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1518733#post1518733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what the Wyrm IS, which is often contradictory. Sometimes the Wyrm is a very humanistic version of evil, which makes no sense in a world where male lions murder the children of rivals, and ducks constantly commit sexual assault, and are considered natural and of the Wyld. Sometimes it's all forces of decay, which means that everything from bacteria to vultures are of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm isn't really anything in a singular sense anymore. It's three fragments trying to understand what went wrong and succumbing to their vices in the meantime, with their emotions becoming Incarnae that seek to keep the whole from healing, else they would cease to exist. However, it can certainly twist a lesser being into another form; typically, this is as a result of a long series of actions wherein said being keeps digging itself in deeper, after some being aligned with the Wyrm notices it do something and decides to poke at it. Presumably, more beings don't respond than not; then, though, every so often, someone is caught up in self-loathing and obsession, making a perfect mark for a bane.<br /> <br /> That's the Wyrm in aggregate - not evil, but a big fan of it. It's tainted and dirty; nothing loves it; it feels nothing but emptiness, and some part of it wants that all to end. It stopped caring about how a long time ago, or lost most of its whole agency in being split into three parts. The functional details don't really differ between those two outcomes. It's feeling around in the dark for a way out, always, from where it was bound. Not much direction from the top, there.<br /> <br /> As for other points, some things to keep in mind<br /> <br /> 1) To emphasize, Gaia and Gaian spirits, what one would consider &quot;natural&quot; are not of the Wyld. They are at a balance point. Only Wyldlings are of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> 2) Beings at this point can end up doing an awful lot of things that are wrong, mistaken, and unpleasant for others. This doesn't automatically make them corrupt; as noted, it takes specific spiritual attention to do so. As such, a lot of the lack of corruption can be attributed to banes either not noticing what animals do or not caring because the bane is attuned to something else or they prefer to play mind games with humans. It could also have to do with, in W:tA, humanity's rejection of Gaia and the Wyld in favor of the Weaver, which can give banes an easy in on any given human.<br /> <br /> 3) Decay of organic matter into new soil is, to be quite honest, so conceptually and mechanically distant from the decay that the Wyrm really likes (of the living spirit) that it might as well be Gaian. As such, no, scavengers and detritivores aren't really aligned with the Wyrm in any sense that matters. The other form of decay, atomic, is elementally of the Wyrm and as such requires no attention from banes to register as being of the Wyrm, but it probably requires some hard, ionizing stuff, because the authors don't count the banana dose as significant enough to register to a Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T16:48:39-07:00","id":1518970,"title":"","content":"It's also important to remember that vampire use their powers to take the best parking spaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T09:26:52-07:00","id":1519037,"title":"","content":"I took it that the hate that the others for the Kindred is that they don't really do anything useful in the world other then feed on the humans and cause death and despair in there wake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T09:51:45-07:00","id":1519041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519037#post1519037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took it that the hate that the others for the Kindred is that they don't really do anything useful in the world other then feed on the humans and cause death and despair in there wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats an interesting point, but one that suggests the Kindred are just an easy target for such hatred.<br /> <br /> Wraiths less predatory but the most likely dead to not give two hoots about the Dictum Mortum and prey on humans are Spectres which are infinity more destructive than the Kindred.<br /> Changelings aren't directly harmful to humans until you get to the Unseelie and Shadow Courts who are just as bad and more often than not leave their victims conpletely broken, they just get away with it due to the Mists.<br /> <br /> And then theres the Garou - a race that actively culled early humanity to such an extent the majority of every generation has the shared inherited psychosis of the Delerium, and some factions tribes would like to see this return and the insinuation in some versions is man eating is not as uncommon or taboo as it should be.<br /> <br /> Think the main point is that unlike the other supernaturals who've all fed or killed humans the kindred just lack a mystical mechanism to hide their transgressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T10:53:46-07:00","id":1519042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519041#post1519041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats an interesting point, but one that suggests the Kindred are just an easy target for such hatred.<br /> <br /> Wraiths less predatory but the most likely dead to not give two hoots about the Dictum Mortum and prey on humans are Spectres which are infinity more destructive than the Kindred.<br /> Changelings aren't directly harmful to humans until you get to the Unseelie and Shadow Courts who are just as bad and more often than not leave their victims conpletely broken, they just get away with it due to the Mists.<br /> <br /> And then theres the Garou - a race that actively culled early humanity to such an extent the majority of every generation has the shared inherited psychosis of the Delerium</div> </div> </div> </div>So long ago that the only records would be cave paintings or maybe some very, very early sculptures; their position would also have made them better thought of by non-agricultural societies that resisted the agricultural ones but subsequently were wiped out or assimilated by the farmers.<br /> <br /> In stark contrast, vampires started draining humans and lulling them into forgetfulness and <i>never stopped</i>. In fact, they never even considered it for a moment; they did take advantage of humans victimizing and casting out other groups of humans, though. Marginalized humans have always been at risk of vampire attack in the WoD, and it would have been most other monsters and workers of spells that shielded them from it if anyone did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and some factions tribes would like to see this return and the insinuation in some versions is man eating is not as uncommon or taboo as it should be. </div> </div> </div>All of them disconnected with the reality of their situation and loathed by Garou as a whole. That's like saying that all vampires are all demon heralds because of the Baali, when in fact they are not, as a whole, given to summoning or other congress with evil, otherworldly beings. They're terrible for entirely different reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think the main point is that unlike the other supernaturals who've all fed or killed humans the kindred just lack a mystical mechanism to hide their transgressions. </div> </div> </div>Vampires probably think that in-character as an excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T11:51:27-07:00","id":1519044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519042#post1519042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marginalized humans have always been at risk of vampire attack in the WoD, and it would have been most other monsters and workers of spells that shielded them from it if anyone did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except canonically that\u2019s not true in the sense of the monsters, Mage and workers of spells yes undoubtably it\u2019s their presence that\u2019s protected humanity.<br /> <br /> Changelings and Wraiths are driven by individual impetus but there\u2019s not an over-riding protection of mankind built into the setting. (Which setting wise if odd given how much both lose if humanity were to become extinct)<br /> <br /> Garou absolutely not, they are the defenders of Gaia not Mankind, aside from self interest in protecting their breeding populations and exceptions such as the Children of Gaia, the Garou are at best indifferent to mankind, usually hold humanity accountable for the harm inflicted on Gaia and worse continuing the cull if you look at the Red Talons and Lupus elements of other tribes.<br /> <br /> As I said there\u2019s no denying the kindreds predation of humanity, however the other supernaturals are displaying some significant double standards by the actions of what their people are doing in this day and age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519042#post1519042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of them disconnected with the reality of their situation and loathed by Garou as a whole. That's like saying that all vampires are all demon heralds because of the Baali, when in fact they are not, as a whole, given to summoning or other congress with evil, otherworldly beings. They're terrible for entirely different reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>So given that there are different stripes of vampire and not all of them guilty of Wyrm activities and in the same context not all Garou are human murderers or man eaters, the Garous universal hatred of the kindred is irrational.<br /> <br /> It can\u2019t be both where the Garou get a universal pass because not all of them are bad, whilst the kindred are marked as universally bad particularly as it\u2019s been discussed in literally hundreds of threads that the Garou are not human, aren\u2019t concerned with human laws, codes of civility or moral compass - so why would the majority be that concerned with a predator that keeps the humans in check.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519042#post1519042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires probably think that in-character as an excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T13:04:32-07:00","id":1519046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519044#post1519044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except canonically that\u2019s not true in the sense of the monsters, Mage and workers of spells yes undoubtably it\u2019s their presence that\u2019s protected humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou likely started off guarding non-agricultural humans and then branched out slightly. That is where a lot of human Kinfolk likely come from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings and Wraiths are driven by individual impetus but there\u2019s not an over-riding protection of mankind built into the setting. (Which setting wise if odd given how much both lose if humanity were to become extinct)<br /> <br /> Garou absolutely not, they are the defenders of Gaia not Mankind, aside from self interest in protecting their breeding populations and exceptions such as the Children of Gaia, the Garou are at best indifferent to mankind, usually hold humanity accountable for the harm inflicted on Gaia and worse continuing the cull if you look at the Red Talons and Lupus elements of other tribes. </div> </div> </div>Gaia made them as a bridge for humans and wolves. They're not interested in helping humans keep up that pedestal, but they also don't feel right just letting humans having their blood taken by vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said there\u2019s no denying the kindreds predation of humanity, however the other supernaturals are displaying some significant double standards by the actions of what their people are doing in this day and age. </div> </div> </div>Not really. At minimum, Garou, Fera, and Changelings have societies that are very aspirational when it comes to altruism and heroism. They might fall short, but there's always that call to do better and make a difference. In contrast, vampires create the status quo and seek to perpetuate it because it gets them all the blood that they can hunt, with little chance that they'll be caught or hunted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So given that there are different stripes of vampire and not all of them guilty of Wyrm activities and in the same context not all Garou are human murderers or man eaters, the Garous universal hatred of the kindred is irrational. </div> </div> </div>Garou don't just not eat people or try to set up the Impergium; they actively discourage that sort of thing among their own. Even the Red Talons are on the same page here; Dying Cubs are going to get killed for fucking up caerns by feeding suffering to them, because that's a clear violation of the last tenet of the Litany. Maneaters and Eaters of the Dead don't advertise, because they would also get summary executions, because, again, there's a specific Litany tenet forbidding Garou human flesh. Going around randomly killing humans because they looked at you funny or you just felt like it, at minimum, is going to result in serious loss of Renown and likely some kind of disciplinary attention.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't leave their own out for the sun for feeding on humans. In fact, trying to prevent that would probably get you staked and left out in the sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can\u2019t be both where the Garou get a universal pass because not all of them are bad, whilst the kindred are marked as universally bad particularly as it\u2019s been discussed in literally hundreds of threads that the Garou are not human, aren\u2019t concerned with human laws, codes of civility or moral compass - so why would the majority be that concerned with a predator that keeps the humans in check. </div> </div> </div>Kindred are nigh-universally bad with some maybe okay exceptions. The others are more neutral or positive with horrid exceptions, in some cases with strong drive to be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T09:29:44-07:00","id":1519261,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires are going left and right making enemies between the other splats. The creation of Camarilla helped the Order of Reason to get the upper hand, and somehow *cough*Tremere*cough* weaken the Traditions. The growing of the cities is destroying the nature, and even the splats self closed, like Changeling and Wraith may suffer with their presence. Of course, the habit of using the rest of the WoD as vintage vitae isn't helping their cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T16:31:33-07:00","id":1519676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518277-the-hatred-the-other-splats-have-for-vampires-is-weird?p=1519261#post1519261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, vampires are going left and right making enemies between the other splats.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is definitely often noted and described that supernatural beings other than Vampires, Ghouls, and Revenants can make choices - as supernatural persons and as fellows of their organisations and teams, for example - that result in them being clearly antagonistic, exploitative, hesitant, isolationistic, ignorant, or selfish.<br /> <br /> For instance Tradition Mages ( be it Choristers or Verbenae ) often can advance their Paradigms without regard for surroundings, the environment, or other persons. They also tend towards pride or arrogance, and in some circumstances they can display lack of understanding, empathy, or refinement.<br /> <br /> Vampires ( and Revenants, and Ghouls ) can definitely be curious and loyal allies and friends, if a person - including a Technocrat or a Tradition Wizard - chooses interact and talk with a Vampiress or a Vampire, and to trust her or him. It is also known and clear that the Kindred do have their own secrets, traditions, laws, wisdom, and culture that they can recount and share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}